**Geometry and search history produced no replicated improvement in predicting NFS smoothness beyond cofactor sizes and small-prime valuations.** The experiment labeled 3,610,064 candidates across 104 balanced semiprimes, with 48 moduli and separate spatial regions held out for testing.

| Smoothness bound | Held-out candidates | Doubly smooth | Relations found at the 20% confirmation budget, model / baseline |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 4,093 | 559,248 | 203 | 136 / 137 |
| 262,139 | 1,118,496 | 27,927 | 11,536 / 11,536 |

At \(B=4{,}093\), the selected model’s log-loss gain was **+0.00000106** per cubic candidate and **−0.00000782** per quartic candidate. This sparse cohort also missed planted odds ratios of 2.01 and 4.06.

I preregistered the higher-bound cohort on fresh moduli to test sensitivity at higher relation prevalence. There, the pipeline **detected the planted 2.01 odds ratio in both families**, at 3.89 and 5.42 cluster standard errors. It recovered 7.02% more planted positives at the same confirmation budget. On real labels, calibration assigned zero weight to every added joint predictor.

The arithmetic checks agreed on every side label. I expanded the higher-bound reference pool before fitting to retain every target under the residue exclusion. The audit verified all 57,761,024 history links across both cohorts. A shuffle preserving each modulus and region’s event rate produced an apparent quartic gain that failed replication. A global shuffle gave zero gain in both families.

Real yield showed no increasing advantage with \(u\), so the measurements provide no evidence for an exponent change. The run took 15.9 minutes from first preregistration through final checks.

